---
/**
 * Chapter 1 — the trend, and the two corrections it has to survive.
 *
 * Lifted out of `pages/index.astro` unchanged when the document became ten
 * routes; the frontmatter here is exactly the part of that page's frontmatter
 * this chapter used.
 */
import TrendChart from "./TrendChart.astro";
import { trend, trendByAirzone, deweatherEvidence } from "../lib/data";
import { n } from "../lib/chart";

const firstYear = trend.years[0];
const lastYear = trend.years[trend.years.length - 1];
const firstValue = trend.all_stations[0] as number;
const lastValue = trend.all_stations[trend.all_stations.length - 1] as number;

const balancedSince = trend.panel.balanced_since as number;
const balancedCount = (trend.panel.balanced_stations as string[]).length;

// How far apart the two ways of computing a national mean actually land, over
// the years where both exist. This is the number that decides whether the
// network-growth caveat changes the story or merely qualifies it.
const overlap = trend.years
  .map((year, i) => ({ year, a: trend.all_stations[i], b: trend.balanced[i] }))
  .filter((row) => row.a != null && row.b != null);
const maxGap = Math.max(...overlap.map((r) => Math.abs((r.a as number) - (r.b as number))));

// --- the second correction: how much of the fall was the weather -----------
// Both lines come from M4's own monthly output, so the gap between them cannot
// be the station set. `weather_share_of_fall` is the level difference across
// this panel; `median_weather_share` is the median of per-station slope
// ratios. Two different aggregations of the same fits, reported together
// because their agreement is worth more than either alone.
const dw = deweatherEvidence;
const dwYears = dw.series.map((r) => r.year);
const dwObserved = dw.series.map((r) => r.observed);
const dwNormalised = dw.series.map((r) => r.normalised);
const dwShare = dw.panel.weather_share_of_fall * 100;
const dwGapNow = dwNormalised[dwNormalised.length - 1] - dwObserved[dwObserved.length - 1];
// The year the observed line drops through the normalised one: before it the
// weather was making things worse than average, after it better.
const dwCrossing = dw.series.find((row, i) => i > 0 && row.observed < row.normalised)?.year;

/*
 * How this chapter's zone figure got to being eight panels.
 *
 * Kept because each step was a real finding and the last one is the point.
 *
 *   1. `var(--c${i % 7})` over eight zones. It wrapped, so zone eight wore
 *      zone one's colour — measured in the built page, the colliding pair were
 *      高屏, the highest series in every year, and a middling zone. Worse, the
 *      index it wrapped was the order the JSON happened to arrive in, so on a
 *      site where hue means concentration, eight lines took their hue from an
 *      array position.
 *   2. Sorted by their own final value and spread across the ramp. Eight into
 *      seven still shares one step, and `Math.round(i * 6 / 7)` deliberately
 *      put that repeat between the two zones adjacent IN CONCENTRATION — the
 *      one place a sequential scale may repeat itself. That call was sound.
 *   3. Coloured by `concentrationColour` of the zone's own value, because rank
 *      is not the quantity the ramp encodes: a zone's colour could move because
 *      a DIFFERENT zone's data moved while the legend still said 15–25.
 *      Honest, and it collapsed eight zones into three bins, because in 2025
 *      the zones genuinely sit in three bins.
 *   4. Dash patterns as a second channel, indexed within the bin rather than
 *      globally — global indexing worked on that day's data only by alignment,
 *      and one more zone in the middle bin would have matched two lines on both
 *      channels.
 *
 * Steps 3 and 4 were both correct and the chart was still unreadable: three
 * colours, three dash patterns, and a legend below the plot, so identifying a
 * zone meant carrying two attributes into a bundle of converging lines eight
 * times. A comment here also claimed each line was labelled at its own end via
 * TrendChart's `.plot-keys`; TrendChart has no `.plot-keys`, and the built page
 * measured zero end labels. Colour was the only identifier, and there were
 * three of it.
 *
 *   5. Eight small panels, one per zone, each named above its own line. That
 *      fixed the identification and broke everything else: the same area cut
 *      into eight, every plot 82px tall, and the colours no better than they
 *      had been. Cutting up a chart that is too small does not make it bigger.
 *   6. One chart again, and each LINE carries its own name and value at its own
 *      end. See the note on `airzoneSeries` below.
 */
/*
 * What the zones actually did, for the sentence that describes them.
 *
 * Computed rather than written down: the sentence this feeds used to assert
 * 「東部與離島本來就低，幾乎沒有下降空間」 while the chart underneath showed 離島
 * falling 15.5 μg/m³ and ending third-highest of eight. A claim about a figure
 * belongs to the figure's own numbers.
 */
const azStats = (trendByAirzone.series as { name: string; mean: (number | null)[] }[])
  .map((s) => {
    const present = s.mean.filter((v): v is number => v != null);
    const first = present[0];
    const last = present[present.length - 1];
    return {
      label: s.name.replace("空品區", ""),
      first,
      last,
      drop: ((first - last) / first) * 100,
    };
  })
  .filter((z) => Number.isFinite(z.drop));

const azSpread = {
  min: Math.min(...azStats.map((z) => z.drop)),
  max: Math.max(...azStats.map((z) => z.drop)),
};
// Highest at the start; the sentence then checks whether it is still highest.
const azTop = azStats.reduce((hi, z) => (z.first > hi.first ? z : hi));
const azStillTop = azStats.every((z) => z.last <= azTop.last);
// Smallest relative fall, and where that leaves it in the current ranking.
const azLeast = azStats.reduce((lo, z) => (z.drop < lo.drop ? z : lo));
const azLeastRank = azStats.filter((z) => z.last > azLeast.last).length + 1;


/*
 * The eight zones, as eight lines that each say their own name.
 *
 * Third attempt at this figure, and the first two failed the same way from
 * opposite ends. One chart with eight lines and a legend underneath could not
 * be read, because identifying a zone meant carrying a colour down to the
 * legend and back. Eight small panels fixed the identification and broke
 * everything else: the same area cut into eight, each plot 82px tall, and the
 * colours no better than before. Slicing a chart that is too small does not
 * make it bigger.
 *
 * What was missing both times is that a line can carry its own name. With the
 * name and the value sitting at the end of each line, nothing on this chart has
 * to be matched to anything beside it — so the legend goes, and colour stops
 * being the identifier it was never able to be at eight.
 *
 * Colour is `concentrationColour` of the zone's own latest value, which puts it
 * in the same three bands the entry map uses. That is deliberately NOT the
 * identifier: the y position already says the level and the label already says
 * the name, so hue is here to group, not to name. Eight distinguishable hues do
 * not exist in this palette and asking for them was the original mistake.
 */
const airzoneSeries = (trendByAirzone.series as {
  name: string;
  years: number[];
  mean: (number | null)[];
}[])
  .map((s) => ({
    key: s.name,
    label: s.name.replace("空品區", ""),
    values: trend.years.map((year) => {
      const at = s.years.indexOf(year);
      return at === -1 ? null : s.mean[at];
    }),
    level: [...s.mean].reverse().find((v) => v != null) ?? -Infinity,
  }))
  .sort((a, b) => b.level - a.level)
  .map((s, i) => ({ ...s, colour: `var(--k${i})` }));


/*
 * Taiwan's PM2.5 annual standard, as it actually was.
 *
 * This was drawn as a flat 15 across 1998–2025, and it is wrong at both ends.
 * PM2.5 was not in 空氣品質標準 at all until it was added on 2012-05-14
 * (民國101年5月14日) at 15 μg/m³ annual and 35 daily; and on 2024-09-30
 * (民國113年9月30日) the annual value was tightened to 12 and the daily to 30.
 * So the old line asserted a limit that did not exist for fourteen of the
 * twenty-eight years it was drawn across, and the wrong limit for the last two.
 *
 * The rule here is "the standard in force at the END of each year", which is
 * the only one that lands cleanly on a series of annual means: 2012 ends under
 * 15, 2024 ends under 12 because the revision took effect that September.
 * Before 2012 the value is null — and a null on this site is drawn as a gap,
 * which is exactly right: there was no limit to draw.
 */
const TW_PM25_ADDED = 2012;
const TW_PM25_TIGHTENED = 2024;
/*
 * Built per chart, from THAT chart's own year axis.
 *
 * It was built once from `trend.years` (1998–2025, 28 entries) and handed to
 * every figure, including the de-weathering one whose axis is `dwYears`
 * (2008–2025, 18). `stepPath` walks the array by index, so index 27 was placed
 * at 27/17 = 159% of a plot that ends at 100 — measured, the guide ran 117px
 * past the right edge of its own plot area. A reference line has to be indexed
 * against the axis it is drawn on.
 */
const taiwanAnnualFor = (years: number[]) =>
  years.map((year) => (year < TW_PM25_ADDED ? null : year < TW_PM25_TIGHTENED ? 15 : 12));

---

<section id="trend" class="page">
  <p class="eyebrow">第一章</p>
  <h1>長期趨勢與氣象校正</h1>

  <p class="lede">
    {firstYear} 到 {lastYear} 年，全台 PM2.5 年均值從 {n(firstValue)} 降到
    {" "}{n(lastValue)} μg/m³。這個數字要能成立，必須先排除一個混淆來源：
    <strong>監測網的測站數在同期間持續增加</strong>。
  </p>

  <p>
    1982 年全台只有 1 個監測站，1999 年才達到 84 站的高峰；PM2.5 更晚，
    1998 年只有 5 個實驗性測點，2005 年才成為全國網絡。
    拿「當年有回報的所有測站」平均，比較的是不同年份的不同地方，
    趨勢裡有一部分來自測站網的組成改變，而非濃度改變。
  </p>

  <p>
    所以這裡畫兩條線。<strong>全部測站</strong>是多數報導引用的數字；
    <strong>固定樣本</strong>只保留 {balancedSince} 年以來每一年都有可比較資料的
    {" "}{balancedCount} 個測站，前後比的是同一批地方。
  </p>

  <figure>
    <TrendChart
      years={trend.years}
      series={[
        {
          key: "all",
          label: "全部測站",
          values: trend.all_stations,
          colour: "var(--k0)",
        },
        {
          key: "balanced",
          label: `固定樣本（${balancedCount} 站，${balancedSince}–）`,
          values: trend.balanced,
          colour: "var(--k1)",
          dash: "5 3",
        },
      ]}
      guides={[
        { values: taiwanAnnualFor(trend.years), label: "台灣年均標準", colour: "var(--taiwan)" },
        { value: 5, label: "WHO 年均指引 5", colour: "var(--who)" },
      ]}
      unit="μg/m³"
    />
    <figcaption>
      全台 PM2.5 年均值。線在中斷處是真的斷開——那一年沒有足以計算的資料，
      而不是數值為零。年覆蓋率低於 75% 的測站年不列入計算。
    </figcaption>
  </figure>

  <div class="note">
    <strong>此項校正未改變結論，而陰性結果同樣需要報告。</strong>
    兩條線在重疊年份的最大差距為 {n(maxGap, 2)} μg/m³。
    {balancedSince} 年以後的下降因此不能歸因於後期加入的測站較為清潔；
    在固定的測站集合上，下降同樣成立。若兩條線分岔，結論就必須修正。
  </div>

  <h2>氣象正規化：分離天氣與排放</h2>

  <p>
    上一個校正量到的差異在誤差範圍內。這一個不是——它改變下降幅度的解讀。
  </p>

  <p>
    同樣一場東北季風，可以把中部的濃度壓下來，也可以把它悶住。
    一年的空氣看起來變好，可能是排放真的少了，也可能只是那幾年的風況比較有利。
    要分開這兩件事，做法是<strong>把天氣抽掉再看一次</strong>：
    用隨機森林學會「這個測站在什麼氣象條件下會有多少 PM2.5」，
    然後對每一個時間點，把氣象變數從整段期間隨機重抽、預測很多次再平均。
    得到的序列可以讀成「如果每一年的天氣都是這 18 年的平均，濃度會是多少」。
  </p>

  <figure>
    <TrendChart
      years={dwYears}
      series={[
        {
          key: "observed",
          label: "實際觀測",
          values: dwObserved,
          colour: "var(--k0)",
        },
        {
          key: "normalised",
          label: "氣象正規化後",
          values: dwNormalised,
          colour: "var(--k1)",
          dash: "5 3",
        },
      ]}
      guides={[{ values: taiwanAnnualFor(dwYears), label: "台灣年均標準", colour: "var(--taiwan)" }]}
      unit="μg/m³"
    />
    <figcaption>
      {dw.panel.n_stations} 個測站、{dw.panel.balanced_since}–{dwYears[dwYears.length - 1]} 年，
      兩條線都出自同一批列。實線是實際量到的；虛線是同一批資料在「平均天氣」下的樣子。
      {dwCrossing && <>兩條線在 {dwCrossing} 年前後交叉。</>}
    </figcaption>
  </figure>

  <div class="note caveat">
    <p>
      <strong>那個交叉點就是答案。</strong>
      實際觀測從 {n(dwObserved[0], 1)} 降到 {n(dwObserved[dwObserved.length - 1], 1)} μg/m³，
      降了 {n(dw.panel.observed_fall, 1)}。但在平均天氣之下，
      同一批測站只從 {n(dwNormalised[0], 1)} 降到 {n(dwNormalised[dwNormalised.length - 1], 1)}，
      降了 {n(dw.panel.normalised_fall, 1)}。
      差額 <strong>{n(dw.panel.observed_fall - dw.panel.normalised_fall, 1)} μg/m³，
      佔了整個下降的 {n(dwShare, 0)}%</strong>。
    </p>
    <p>
      換句話說：{dwYears[0]} 年的天氣讓空氣看起來比排放本身更差，
      {dwYears[dwYears.length - 1]} 年的天氣讓它看起來比排放本身更好
      （現在這個差距是 {n(dwGapNow, 1)} μg/m³）。
      <strong>把兩者相加，就是那條實線比虛線陡的原因。</strong>
    </p>
  </div>

  <p>
    這個比例還可以用完全不同的方式再問一次。上面是<strong>全國面板的水準差</strong>；
    另一種是對 {dw.n_significant} 個測站各自估斜率，再取「天氣佔比」的中位數——
    那個答案是 <strong>{n(dw.median_weather_share * 100, 1)}%</strong>，
    與 {n(dwShare, 1)}% 相差不到 1.5 個百分點。
    兩種聚合方式互相獨立，一致比任何單一數字更值得相信。
    跨測站的 p10–p90 也只有 {n(dw.weather_share_p10 * 100, 0)}–{n(dw.weather_share_p90 * 100, 0)}%——
    {dw.n_significant} 個獨立配適的模型落在同一個窄帶裡，
    是因為整座島共用同一套季風通風機制。
  </p>

  <div class="note">
    <p>
      <strong>這不是因果歸因，界線要劃清楚。</strong>
      {dw.caveat}
    </p>
    <p>
      另有一點需要說明：正規化後的序列在<strong>年內幾乎是平的</strong>，
      因為重抽樣連日序與小時一起換掉了，季節循環也跟著被移除。
      那是預期行為，所以這張圖只畫年度——畫成逐月會看起來像繪圖錯誤。
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>各空品區</h2>
  {/*
    Rewritten because the figure underneath contradicted it.

    It said 「中部與雲嘉南的起點高、降幅大；東部與離島本來就低，幾乎沒有下降空間」.
    Measured from the same file the chart is drawn from: every zone fell between
    50.1% and 71.8%, so 「幾乎沒有下降空間」 is true of none of them — 離島 fell
    15.5 μg/m³ and 東部 60.5%. 離島 is not 「本來就低」 either: it started at 30.92,
    above three other zones, and it now ends THIRD-HIGHEST of the eight. And the
    zone that best fits the sentence's own first clause, 高屏 — highest start,
    largest fall — was not named at all.

    The figures below are computed, so the sentence cannot drift from the chart
    again.
  */}
  <p>
    下降不是均勻的，但沒有一區例外：八個空品區的降幅都落在
    {" "}{n(azSpread.min, 0)}% 到 {n(azSpread.max, 0)}% 之間。
    起點最高的{azTop.label}降幅也最大（{n(azTop.first, 1)} → {n(azTop.last, 1)} μg/m³）
    {azStillTop && <>，而且排序幾乎沒有動：它當年最高，現在仍然最高</>}。
    真正換了位置的是{azLeast.label}——它的降幅最小（{n(azLeast.drop, 0)}%），
    於是從中段升到全台第 {azLeastRank} 高。
  </p>

  <figure>
    <TrendChart
      years={trend.years}
      series={airzoneSeries}
      guides={[{ values: taiwanAnnualFor(trend.years), label: "台灣年均標準", colour: "var(--taiwan)" }]}
      unit="μg/m³"
      height={620}
      {/* No end labels: eight of them stacked at the right edge was the wall
          this figure just came out of. The names live in the in-plot legend,
          which places itself wherever the eight lines left room. */}
      keys="none"
      notesAt="left"
    />
    <figcaption>
      各空品區 PM2.5 年均值。每條線在自己的末端寫著自己的名字與 2025 年的值，
      並以自己的顏色連回線上，所以不需要對照圖例。八個顏色是為了「彼此分得開」解出來的
      （最接近的一對 dE00 18.9，含綠色盲與紅色盲模擬），與濃度分帶無關。
      同樣只採計年覆蓋率 ≥ 75% 的測站年。
    </figcaption>
  </figure>
</section>
